---
description: Personal data, credentials and external side-effect boundaries
alwaysApply: true
---

# Personal data and secrets

- Keep OCR and extraction local. Never upload source documents, OCR text, real identifiers or screenshots containing personal data to third-party cloud services.
- Use synthetic data in tests. Do not put real names, tax IDs, insurance IDs, birth dates, addresses or document text in fixtures, logs, commits or reports.
- Keep credentials in `.env`; do not display the file. Do not commit `.env` or browser session profiles. If a credential is found in a tracked example/history, remove it from the current file and notify the owner that rotation is required.

# Absolute prohibition on real SRO changes

Never create, edit, delete, submit or save a real SROArbitr record. Do not run `run --live`, click Save/Send, or click Add where it may create a draft. This applies even if a test, user story or old documentation suggests doing so. Use isolated mocks/fakes and disposable local DBs.

Read-only browsing is allowed only after the specific action's side effects are understood. Test filling is allowed only when the form is proven not to autosave or create a record. Never retry an SRO job with an uncertain external outcome before read-only reconciliation.

Do not bypass KAD/MKAD challenges, CAPTCHA, rate limits or access controls. Stop and report the acquisition failure.
